            <ArticleTitle>Barbados Blackbelly: the Caribbean ovine genetic resource.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11250-017-1475-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovine production is one of the most important activities in animal production in tropical regions. The Barbados Blackbelly, a very interesting genetic resource, particularly well adapted to a harsh home environment in the humid tropics of the Caribbean. This review concerns this breed. It comprises aspects related to the breed history and standards and most importantly its reproductive and productive performances and gastrointestinal parasite tolerance in the Caribbean, North America and Central America and their introduction and use in crossbred trials in other regions of the tropics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
